.TH LINTO 1 "October 2026" "linto" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linto \- dispatch command-line tools from the Linux Tools collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linto
.RI [ --help ]
.br
.B linto
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B linto
.I group command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B linto help
.RI [ group ] [ command ]
.br
.B linto completion
.RI { bash | zsh | fish }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linto
is a command dispatcher for the local Linux Tools collection. It locates tools
relative to the
.B linto
launcher, so commands can be run from any working directory. A tool receives
the arguments supplied after its command name.
.PP
With no arguments or with
.BR --help ,
.B linto
prints the available groups and their commands. Running a group by itself
lists its commands. Each command can be run as
.B "linto GROUP COMMAND"
or as the shorthand
.BR "linto COMMAND" .
.SH GROUPS
The current command groups are
.BR awk ,
.BR beta ,
.BR bibtex ,
.BR internal ,
.BR launch ,
.BR quarto ,
and
.BR utils .
Run a group by itself to list its commands. The
.B launch
group contains the Zed launcher. Use a group followed by a command to run a
tool explicitly, for example
.BR "linto utils prettyprint" .
All commands can also be invoked without the group when their names are unique.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help [GROUP] [COMMAND]
Print the general tool guide with no arguments. With a command name, display
that tool's help; a group may be specified to select the command explicitly.
For most commands this runs the tool with
.BR --help ;
some commands provide dispatcher-specific help instead.
.TP
.B completion SHELL
Print shell completion setup instructions for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
or
.BR fish .
This prints instructions; it does not modify shell configuration files.
.TP
.I command [arguments ...]
Run a tool by its command name, optionally without its group.
.TP
.I group command [arguments ...]
Run a tool from the specified group. The tool's standard input, output, error,
and exit status are passed through.
.PP
The alias
.B slug
runs
.BR stripaccents .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Print the usage summary when given as the first argument. To request help for a
specific tool, use
.B "linto COMMAND --help"
or
.BR "linto help GROUP COMMAND" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The dispatcher exits with status 0 when it successfully prints its own help or
completion instructions. Invalid dispatcher usage, an unsupported completion
shell, or an unknown command results in status 2. For a dispatched command,
.B linto
returns that command's exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the available commands:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
List commands in a group:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto quarto
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run a tool with or without its group:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto render --help
linto quarto render --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open a file with the Zed tool:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto zed Makefile
.RE
.fi
.PP
Print the Bash completion setup line:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto completion bash
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I linto
The command dispatcher.
.TP
.I linto-guide
The general guide shown by
.BR "linto help" .
.TP
.I completions/linto.bash
.TQ
.I completions/linto.zsh
.TQ
.I completions/linto.fish
Shell completion definitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fish (1)
